erything after that point. I'm implementing the Rust version by using `partition_point` to find where the offset threshold is, then truncating the queue to keep only the nodes that should be retained. Now I'm moving on to the bandwidth estimation method on the Path struct. Finishing the bandwidth estimation logic and then considering how to adapt this for Rust, where time values are represented as `Instant` objects rather than raw `u64` integers. I need to figure out how `Instant` arithmetic works in this codebase—specifically how to subtract two `Instant` values to get a duration. Let me look at how other parts of the code handle `Instant` operations, like in the bandwidth and RTT calculations, to understand the pattern.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1988,"cache_read_input_tokens":52829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1988},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22223bee-eee6-4df4-be23-f562ef79ea05","uuid":"bddbb6d2-a6ee-45c5-83c2-9a2db9c068f5"}
