{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016krBuHFjiqNFq3RubDU8wM","type":"tool_result","content":"6890\timpl Connection {\n6891\t    /// Estimate the number of packets in the congestion window, used to\n6892\t    /// derive the ACK-frequency gap.  Returns at least 2.\n6893\t    ///\n6894\t    /// When ACK frequency is negotiated the window packet count comes from\n6895\t    /// `cwin / send_mtu`; otherwise it is derived from\n6896\t    /// `data_rate × smoothed_rtt / send_mtu` (rounded up).\n6897\t    ///\n6898\t    /// C: `picoquic_compute_packets_in_window` (`frames.c:2974-2995`)\n6899\t    fn compute_packets_in_window(&self, data_rate: u64) -> u64 {\n6900\t        let nb_packets = if let Some(path) = self.paths.first() {\n6901\t            let send_mtu = path.send_mtu as u64;\n6902\t            if self.is_ack_frequency_negotiated {\n6903\t                path.cwin / send_mtu.max(1)\n6904\t            } else {\n6905\t                let rtt_bytes_times_1000000 = data_rate.saturating_mul(path.smoothed_rtt.ticks());\n6906\t                let rtt_packets_times_1000000 = rtt_bytes_times_1000000 / send_mtu.max(1);\n6907\t                rtt_packets_times_1000000.div_ceil(1_000_000)\n6908\t            }\n6909\t        } else {\n6910\t            0\n6911\t        };\n6912\t        nb_packets.max(2)\n6913\t    }\n6914\t\n6915\t    /// Compute the ACK-gap from the number of packets in the window and the\n6916\t    /// data rate.  This is a private helper called by\n6917\t    /// [`Connection::compute_ack_gap_and_delay`].\n6918\t    ///\n6919\t    /// C: `picoquic_compute_ack_gap` (`frames.c:2997-3045`)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22223bee-eee6-4df4-be23-f562ef79ea05","uuid":"ba4fc84c-b03c-4f7d-a1df-52cfb273eea8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T06:25:58.204Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/internal.rs","content":"impl Connection {\n    /// Estimate the number of packets in the congestion window, used to\n    /// derive the ACK-frequency gap.  Returns at least 2.\n    ///\n    /// When ACK frequency is negotiated the window packet count comes from\n    /// `cwin / send_mtu`; otherwise it is derived from\n    /// `data_rate × smoothed_rtt / send_mtu` (rounded up).\n    ///\n    /// C: `picoquic_compute_packets_in_window` (`frames.c:2974-2995`)\n    fn compute_packets_in_window(&self, data_rate: u64) -> u64 {\n        let nb_packets = if let Some(path) = self.paths.first() {\n            let send_mtu = path.send_mtu as u64;\n            if self.is_ack_frequency_negotiated {\n                path.cwin / send_mtu.max(1)\n            } else {\n                let rtt_bytes_times_1000000 = data_rate.saturating_mul(path.smoothed_rtt.ticks());\n                let rtt_packets_times_1000000 = rtt_bytes_times_1000000 / send_mtu.max(1);\n                rtt_packets_times_1000000.div_ceil(1_000_000)\n            }\n        } else {\n            0\n        };\n        nb_packets.max(2)\n    }\n\n    /// Compute the ACK-gap from the number of packets in the window and the\n    /// data rate.  This is a private helper called by\n    /// [`Connection::compute_ack_gap_and_delay`].\n    ///\n    /// C: `picoquic_compute_ack_gap` (`frames.c:2997-3045`)","numLines":30,"startLine":6890,"totalLines":11671}}}
